{"from": "claim:ac-18-08-crispus-believed", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:1-corinthians-1-14", "note": "1 Corinthians 1:14: Paul baptized 'Crispus and Gaius' - the same Corinthian convert in Paul's own letter; a cross-reference, not external evidence."}
{"from": "claim:ac-18-17-sosthenes-beaten", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:1-corinthians-1-1", "note": "1 Corinthians 1:1 names 'Sosthenes the brother' with Paul - possibly the beaten synagogue ruler, later a co-sender; a cross-reference, not external evidence."}
{"from": "claim:ac-18-02-priscilla-wife", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:1-corinthians-16-19", "note": "1 Corinthians 16:19: 'Aquila and Priscilla greet you much in the Lord, together with the assembly that is in their house' - the same couple from Paul's own letter; a cross-reference, not external evidence."}
{"from": "claim:ac-18-02-jews-in-pontus", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:1-peter-1-1", "note": "1 Peter 1:1 addresses 'the Dispersion in Pontus, Galatia...' - Jews of Pontus in the diaspora; a cross-reference, not external evidence."}
{"from": "claim:ac-18-02-claudius-expulsion", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:josephus-ant-18-81-84-rome-jews", "note": "Josephus Ant. 18.81-84 records the earlier 19 CE expulsion of Jews from Rome under Tiberius; do not conflate it with Claudius's edict."}
{"from": "claim:ac-18-06-shook-garments", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-10-14-shake-dust", "note": "The same gesture family: shaking out garments/dust against those who reject the message (Matt 10:14); Acts 18:6 shakes out his clothing against the Corinthian Jews."}
